<manifest xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">
  <!--
    Permissions intentionally NOT declared here. BLUETOOTH_CONNECT /
    BLUETOOTH_SCAN (+ legacy BLUETOOTH/BLUETOOTH_ADMIN + ACCESS_FINE_LOCATION
    maxSdkVersion=30 for classic inquiry) are declared at the app level in
    apps/mobile/app.json so there's a single source of truth (see
    plugins/withNearbyWifiNeverForLocation.js).

    The FOREGROUND_SERVICE_* + POST_NOTIFICATIONS permissions the native
    KaataForegroundService needs are declared at app level in app.json.

    The <service> itself is declared via the app-level config plugin
    plugins/withKaataForegroundService.js (NOT here) so it lands directly in the
    prebuild's app manifest — verifiable + present in every build regardless of
    module-manifest merge timing (a stale prebuild once shipped without it).
  -->
</manifest>
